    <statement><p>If <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m> are arbitrary polynomials of degree at most 2, then the mapping 
<me>\langle f,g\rangle = f(-2)g(-2) + f(0)g(0) + f(1)g(1)</me> 
defines an inner product in <m>P_2</m>. 
Use this inner product to find <m>\langle f,g\rangle</m>, <m>\| f \|</m>, <m>\| g \|</m>, and the angle 
<m>\alpha_{f,g}</m> between <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m> for 
<me>f(x) = 3 x^2 + 2 x  - 1 \ \mbox{ and } \ g(x) = 3 x^2  - 5 x + 9.</me></p>
<p><m>\langle f,g\rangle =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>\| f \| =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,</p>
<p><m>\| g \| =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,</p>
<p><m>\alpha_{f,g} =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/>.</p>
</statement>
